<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="column english">
            <h1>Why is the Sky Blue?</h1>
            <h2>For a 3‑Year‑Old Toddler</h2>
            <p>The sky looks blue because the sunlight loves to play hide‑and‑seek with tiny invisible things in the air. When sunlight comes in, the blue part of the light likes to bounce around the most, so we see a lot of blue when we look up.</p>
            <h2>For a High School Teenager</h2>
            <p>The sky appears blue due to a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight is made up of many colors, each with a different wavelength. Shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) scatter more easily when they collide with molecules and small particles in Earth's atmosphere. Our eyes are more sensitive to blue than violet, and some violet light is absorbed by the upper atmosphere, so we perceive the sky as blue.</p>
            <h2>For a Physics PhD</h2>
            <p>The blue color of the sky results from elastic scattering of photons by atmospheric constituents much smaller than the wavelength of visible light—primarily N₂ and O₂ molecules. The scattering intensity follows the Rayleigh law, \(I \propto \frac{1}{\lambda^4}\), leading to a strong wavelength dependence. Integrating the scattered solar spectrum over the solid angle of the sky and weighting by the photopic response of the human visual system yields a predominant blue hue. Minor contributions from Mie scattering by aerosols and the absorption of violet light by ozone further refine the perceived color.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="column chinese">
            <h1>天空为什么是蓝色？</h1>
            <h2>对于3岁的幼儿</h2>
            <p>天空看起来是蓝色的，因为阳光喜欢和空气中微小的看不见的东西玩躲猫猫。当阳光进入时，光的蓝色部分喜欢到处弹跳，所以我们抬头看时看到很多蓝色。</p>
            <h2>对于高中生</h2>
            <p>天空呈蓝色是由于一种叫做瑞利散射的现象。阳光由许多颜色组成，每种颜色有不同的波长。较短的波长（蓝色和紫色）在地球大气中与分子和小颗粒碰撞时更容易散射。我们的眼睛对蓝色比对紫色更敏感，并且一些紫光被上层大气吸收，因此我们感知天空为蓝色。</p>
            <h2>对于物理学博士</h2>
            <p>天空的蓝色是由可见光波长远大于的大气成分（主要是N₂和O₂分子）对光子的弹性散射导致的。散射强度遵循瑞利定律，\(I \propto \frac{1}{\lambda^4}\)，导致强烈的波长依赖性。将天空立体角上的散射太阳谱积分并按照人眼视觉系统的光敏感响应加权，得到主要的蓝色调。气溶胶的米散射以及臭氧对紫光的吸收的微小贡献进一步细化了感知的颜色。</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>"}

